The legal texts and the data about them come from the Centralised Database of Legal Information of the Ministry of
Justice of the Kyrgyz Republic:

  Источник: Централизованный банк данных правовой информации Министерства юстиции Кыргызской Республики,
  https://cbd.minjust.gov.kg

Under the Kyrgyz law on copyright (Закон Кыргызской Республики от 14 января 1998 года № 6 "Об авторском праве и
смежных правах", статья 8), "Не являются объектами авторского права: официальные документы (законы, постановления,
решения и т.п.), а также их официальные переводы". The Constitutions and laws in this repository are texts of that
kind.

REUSE OF THE DATABASE IS UNCLEAR. cbd.minjust.gov.kg and its API publish no terms of use and no licence (checked
2026-10-28; robots.txt has an empty Disallow and no Crawl-delay). The database's own arrangement, headers and notes may
be protected even where the texts are not. Until the terms are clarified this repository stays PRIVATE.

Changes made by Lexifina: each edition's HTML was converted to one Markdown file per article (one line per
paragraph); words broken at the end of a printed line were joined; the database's status banner over past editions was
left out; spacing was collapsed; and the editions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made each
change. The wording of the law was not changed. The Ministry of Justice of the Kyrgyz Republic does not endorse this
repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
